/TU (Part 8\056 Civil Surgeon Worksheet\056 2\056 Physical or Mental Disorders With Associated Harmful Behavior\056 Include here any physical or mental disorders with current associated harmful behavior or history of associated harmful behavior judged likely to recur\056  This category of physical or mental disorders includes any diagnosis of substance\055use disorders that involve any substance that is not listed in Schedule I\054 II\054 III\054 IV\054 or V of section 202 of the Controlled Substances Act \050for example\054 diagnosis of an alcohol\055use disorder\051\056  Diagnose mental disorders according to the diagnostic criteria in the most recent edition of the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual \050DSM\051 or another authoritative source\054 as determined by the director of the CDC\056  Diagnose physical disorders according to the diagnostic criteria in the most recent edition of the World Health Organization\047s Manual of the International Classification of Diseases\054 Injuries\054 and Causes of Death \050ICD\051 or another authoritative source as determined by the director of the CDC\056  See the CDC\047s Technical Instructions for Civil Surgeons for more information\056  B\056 Remarks\072  Include diagnosis\054 likelihood of recurrence of the harmful behavior\054 therapy given\054 and any counseling or referrals\056  If you need extra space to complete this section\054 use the space provided in Part 11\056 Additional Information\056)
/Type /Annot
>>
endobj
