/E (Part 8\056 Civil Surgeon Worksheet\056 3\056 Drug Abuse \057 Drug Addiction\056 The U\056S\056 Department of Health and Human Services \050DHHS\051 sets the medical guidelines for determining drug abuse and drug addiction\056  The terms are defined at 42 C F R 34\0562\050h\051 and \050i\051\056 Include here any diagnosis of drug abuse or drug addiction\056 \042Drug abuse or drug addiction\042 is \042current substance use disorder mild\054 moderate or severe\216 but only with respect to substances listed in Schedule I\054 II\054 III\054 IV\054 or V of section 202 of the Controlled Substances Act\056 Make the diagnosis according to the diagnostic criteria in the most current edition of the DSM\054 or by another authoritative source as determined by the director of the CDC\056 You may also make a diagnosis of full remission\054 according to the diagnostic criteria in the most current edition of the DSM or another authoritative source as determined by the director of the CDC\056  See the CDC\047s Technical Instructions for Civil Surgeons for more information\056 A\056 Findings\056 4\056 Select Substance \050Drug\051 Addiction in Full Remission\054 listed in section 202 of the Controlled Substances Act\054 Class B\056)
